 ## Context occupancy measurement
 
+The Provider Registry owns sparse capacity evidence independently of its completed runtime
+configuration. API and native model factories capture that same evidence: an observed or explicit
+capacity, or an admitted selectable window, remains fixed for the accepted model; absent evidence
+is `null`, even when its internal working budget uses the existing fallback. Native model binding
+must not promote that fallback to a confirmed ModelComplete denominator. Existing complete-only
+Registry callers retain their legacy configured-capacity behavior. Refresh affects newly created
+models, while durable observed/manual fields retain their original writer and cold-reopen path.
+Native response metadata and reported usage remain provider observations, never backfilled from
+the working budget. Each new main-turn ModelComplete publishes a known capacity or explicit
+`null`; V4 clears the current model's old denominator on `null`, while absent fields in legacy
+events remain compatible. Late results from an old model and sidecars cannot change the current
+capacity. Historical usage and SQLite records remain intact. No configuration field, account access, migration or second capacity owner
+is introduced. `packages/core/test/native-model-capacity.test.ts` exercises actual Registry,
+frozen API/native factories and Host observations using isolated repositories and a scripted
+native port; it starts no CLI or provider inference.
+The selectable-window fixture proves Host admission, freezing and publication only. It does not
+prove that a native backend changes its own working window; that requires its executor binding.
+
+Named bundled rules that declare capacities/capabilities or supported/default effort carry
+optional `evidenceModelIds`: exact published model IDs within
+that existing rule, not account membership or another catalog. The bundled scope is checked
+against the installed Pi 1.0.1 static chat IDs and existing fixed template IDs. A scoped rule
+resolves only those exact IDs, so arbitrary future/private suffixes cannot acquire its capacity,
+capabilities. Pure wire-map rules retain their compatibility behavior for future/alias IDs and
+do not supply capacity/capability evidence. Catchall rules retain their universal internal/wire behavior and
+carry no scope. Unscoped legacy regex remains an internal recommendation, while only a literal
+exact match can supply evidence. Actual observations, explicit personal corrections and exact
+template/provider rules keep their existing order. Parse, compose and JSON encoding preserve
+the same immutable scope field; no stored personal data is migrated or inferred from a name.
+
 The existing V4 Session usage projection owns optional `contextWindow.measurement`: source
 (`provider-usage`, `runtime-estimate`, `unknown`), state (`current`, `stale`), observation time,
 known request provider/model identity, and stale reason (`model-change`, `compaction`, `restored`).
@@ -141,3 +171,12 @@ no usage and unpriced models leave the payment unallocated. Only observed Fleet
 ongoing billing periods are provisional and mixed currencies are never summed. Display per-model
 cache ratio as summed reported cache reads divided by the corresponding reported total input.
 Token popup retains original context/allowance shape; request/cost analytics lives in Usage only.
+
+## Model tool capability projection
+
+The existing `getTools(model)` owner projects no tool declarations for an explicit false tool
+capability. Native factories preserve an explicit negative correction too. Text-only rounds
+still use the original Host/Pi, request, receipt and usage path.
+The same empty set governs context/Skill discovery and effect admission; a hallucinated call
+obtains neither permission nor an effect. Unknown/true capability and no-model local catalogues
+retain their existing behavior. Actual SDK JSON/SSE fixtures cover all three API formats and reopen.
